<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Stochastic Gridworld</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stochasticity is introduced by allowing the environment, with a probability of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>%, to move the agent randomly either to the left or right relative to its intended direction (i.e. with a probability of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>% to the left and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>% to the right).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F6.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05996v1/figures/gridworld/empowerment_5_steps_stochastic_easy.png" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/413;" width="476" height="413" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F6.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05996v1/figures/gridworld/empowerment_5_steps_stochastic_hard.png" id="A1.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/411;" width="476" height="411" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><math id="A1.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-steps empowerment-values of the stochastic gridworld environment. In the left environment the agent randomly moves to the left or right with a probability of <math id="A1.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>% and in the right environment the agent randomly moves to the left or right with a probability of <math id="A1.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>%. Otherwise the agent moves in the intended direction of the chosen action.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Experiments</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each episode in our gridworld environment consists of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> steps. Rewards are normalized to the range <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, with the goal state assigned a reward of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. In empowerment-maximization environments, the goal state corresponds to the state with maximal empowerment. We calculate discounted empowerment with a discount factor of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.95</annotation></semantics></math> and a time horizon of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=32</annotation></semantics></math> steps. To ensure exploration during later fine-tuning, we penalize low entropy of the policy during pre-training and fine-tuning. All our networks are trained using the Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> with default parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate each agent every <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25,000</annotation></semantics></math> environment steps for <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> (REINFORCE and AC) or <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math> (PPO and DQN) episodes. The graphs in our plots show the mean return and the standard deviation of the mean over the evaluation results of all runs of the experiment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our implementation is based on JAX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>. PPO and DQN agents are trained using NVIDIA V100 GPUs, with each training run requiring approximately two hours using a single GPU. We utilize the Stable-Baselines (SBX) framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite> for these two algorithms. All other algorithms are executed on CPUs, with each run completing in approximately <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>45</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45</annotation></semantics></math> minutes (for pre-training and fine-tuning). Across all experiments, we allocate <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math> GB of memory; however, lower memory usage may suffice depending on the specific algorithm.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Training of the Capacity-Achieving Policy</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The capacity-achieving policy is the output of the Blahut-Arimoto algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>. The algorithm provides only action distributions for each state independently. We pre-train our neural network policies by approximating these distributions through behavior cloning from sampled actions, enabling effective subsequent fine-tuning.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Hyperparameters</h3>

<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="A1.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Overview of the hyperparameters for REINFORCE.</span></figcaption>
